# Test: test cases document (`y-tst-test-cases`)

Use this rule when a work item needs a **Test Cases** document: a concise, executable list of scenarios QA can run against an existing **Testing Criteria** doc.

**Criteria vs test cases:**

- **Testing Criteria** (`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-testing-criteria.mdc`) — what must be true (Pass/Fail requirements).
- **Test Cases** (this rule) — how to exercise those requirements (steps, evidence).

Do **not** duplicate acceptance criteria prose here; **reference criterion numbers** in each case **Goal** when traceability helps.

## When to use

- After `docs/<JIRA-KEY>/testing-criteria.md` exists (or in the same task once criteria are defined).
- QA handoff, regression planning, or manual E2E prep for behavior changes.
- User asks for “test cases for this task/ticket” at document level (not a single ad-hoc case).

For **one standalone test case** in chat only, use **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc`** directly.

Do **not** use this rule for E2E run reports (`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc`).

## Artifact location

- Save under **`docs/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md`** (for example `docs/VAP-2291/test-cases.md`).
- One file per work item unless the user specifies a different path.
- Track the file in git when created for implementation work.

## Document title

```markdown
# VAP-2291 - Test Cases - 20260730-1612
```

**Pattern:** `<JIRA-KEY> - Test Cases - <YYYYMMDD-HHMM>`

Use the **local** date and time when the document is **written or last substantively updated** (24-hour time, minute precision).

## Header block (required, immediately after H1)

```markdown
**Work item:** [<JIRA-KEY>](https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/<JIRA-KEY>)
**Criteria:** [testing-criteria.md](testing-criteria.md)
**Audience:** QA
```

Use a relative link to the sibling criteria file in the same `docs/<JIRA-KEY>/` folder.

---

## Document body

The body contains **only test cases** — no acceptance criteria tables, no definition-of-done section, no implementation file lists.

### Test case entries

Each test case is one `###` subsection, separated by `---` from the next.

**Heading format:**

```markdown
### TST-<AREA>-<NNN> — <Short Title In Title Case>
```

- **Code and title rules:** follow **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc`** (`TST-<AREA>-<NNN>`, unique within the document).
- **AREA examples:** `BUG`, `WO`, `CASE`, `REG` — pick one area prefix per work item when possible.
- **Numbering:** `001`, `002`, … in execution priority order (core paths first, edge cases later).

### Fields per test case (required)

Every test case **must** include all fields from **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc`**, using **bold labels**:

```markdown
### TST-<AREA>-<NNN> — <Short Title>

- **Goal:** <what this validates; reference criteria numbers when useful, e.g. “criteria 1, 4”>
- **Preconditions:**
  - <condition 1>
  - <condition 2>
- **Steps:**
  - <step 1>
  - <step 2>
- **Expected result:**
  - <measurable pass behavior>
  - <optional second bullet>
- **Evidence to collect:**
  - <field names, ids, transcript snippets>
```

**Per-case rules** (from `.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc`, applied here):

- Short bullets; one action per step.
- **Expected result** must be pass/fail measurable (no vague “works correctly”).
- **Evidence** must be practical (for ResiRoo: `Response`, `State`, `Title`, `IsEmergency`, `Evidence`, conversation id, transcript).
- Wording may allow **semantic equivalence** when criteria doc says so — state that in expected result only when relevant.

Separate each test case with:

```markdown
---
```

Do not add a horizontal rule before the first test case or after the last.

---

## Coverage guidance

When authoring from a Testing Criteria doc:

1. Read all numbered criterion groups (`### 1.` … `### N.`).
2. Add at least one test case per **critical** criterion group; combine related groups in one case when efficient.
3. Include **positive** paths (expected routing/behavior) and **boundary** paths (urgent wording, photos already sent, cannot send photos, handoff timing).
4. Prefer **multi-turn** steps when criteria allow behavior across messages (not everything required in turn 1).
5. Keep the set **concise** — omit redundant cases that differ only in wording.

Typical case count: **~6–12** for a focused behavior change; fewer if scope is narrow.

---

## Style

- **B2 English:** clear, executable, professional.
- **Scope:** test cases only; no product essays or code paths.
- **Title Case:** test case titles in `###` headings.
- **Resident messages:** write natural opener text in **Steps** (quoted or after “Report:”).
- **Environment:** mention MP (Testing) or Local in preconditions when relevant; do not duplicate full E2E runbooks (see `.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e.mdc` at execution time).

---

## Quality checks (before handoff)

- [ ] Header links to correct Jira key and `testing-criteria.md`.
- [ ] Every case has a unique `TST-<AREA>-<NNN>` code.
- [ ] Every case includes Goal, Preconditions, Steps, Expected result, Evidence (bold labels).
- [ ] Each case maps to at least one acceptance criterion (named in Goal).
- [ ] No acceptance criteria tables or definition-of-done duplicated from the criteria doc.
- [ ] File tracked in git.

